    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai` CLI where the `--ci` flag was not being passed through to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe main `frai` program had a global `--ci` option defined. When running `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was consuming the `--ci` flag as a global option before it could be passed to the spawned `frai-gate` process.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-754) to capture all raw command-line arguments after 'gate' using `process.argv` instead of relying on the parsed `args` from Commander.js. This ensures all arguments, including the `--ci` flag, are passed to the spawned `frai-gate` process.\n\n**Testing:**\n\u2705 Confirmed that running `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the workflow file that was previously missing)\n\nThe rebuild was successful with `pnpm --filter frai build`, and the fix is now in place.",
